---
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ArticleContent from '@/components/articles/ArticleContent.astro';
import ArticleFAQ from '@/components/articles/ArticleFAQ.astro';
import ArticleStats from '@/components/articles/ArticleStats.astro';
import FreeConsultationForm from '@/components/home/FreeConsultationForm.astro';
import Testimonials from '@/components/home/Testimonials.astro';
import LocationMap from '@/components/home/LocationMap.astro';

const faqItems = [
  {
    question: "What should I do immediately after a pedestrian accident?",
    answer: "Seek medical attention immediately, even if injuries seem minor. Call 911 to report the accident and obtain a police report. If possible, gather contact information from witnesses and the driver, take photos of the scene, and document your injuries. Contact an experienced pedestrian accident attorney as soon as possible to protect your rights and preserve critical evidence."
  },
  {
    question: "Who is liable in a pedestrian accident case?",
    answer: "Liability typically falls on the driver if they were negligent—such as failing to yield at a crosswalk, driving distracted, speeding, or violating traffic laws. However, other parties may also be liable, including property owners if poor maintenance contributed to the accident, or government entities if inadequate pedestrian infrastructure played a role. Our attorneys thoroughly investigate each case to identify all responsible parties."
  },
  {
    question: "What compensation can I recover after a pedestrian accident?",
    answer: "Victims may recover compensation for medical expenses, lost wages, future medical care, pain and suffering, emotional distress, permanent disability, and loss of quality of life. In cases involving severe negligence, punitive damages may also be available. At Logeman & Iafrate, P.C., we fight to secure full and fair compensation that addresses both your immediate and long-term needs."
  },
  {
    question: "What if the driver who hit me fled the scene?",
    answer: "Hit-and-run accidents present unique challenges, but you still have legal options. You may be able to recover compensation through your own no-fault insurance policy or uninsured motorist coverage, potentially including policies held by other household members. Our attorneys work swiftly to identify all available insurance resources and help you access the benefits you need for medical expenses and other losses."
  },
  {
    question: "How long do I have to file a pedestrian accident claim in Michigan?",
    answer: "Michigan law imposes strict deadlines for filing personal injury claims. Generally, you have three years from the date of the accident to file a lawsuit, but certain circumstances may shorten this timeframe. Additionally, no-fault insurance benefits must be claimed within one year of the accident. Prompt action is essential—contact our firm immediately to ensure your rights are protected and all deadlines are met."
  },
  {
    question: "Will I have to go to court for my pedestrian accident case?",
    answer: "Many pedestrian accident cases are resolved through negotiation and settlement without going to trial. However, at Logeman & Iafrate, P.C., we are always trial-ready and not afraid to take your case to court if necessary to secure the compensation you deserve. Our 45+ years of experience and proven track record demonstrate our commitment to fighting for justice at every stage of the legal process."
  }
];
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Ann Arbor Pedestrian Accident Lawyers | Logeman & Iafrate, P.C."
  description="Experienced Ann Arbor pedestrian accident attorneys at Logeman & Iafrate, P.C. fight for victims injured by negligent drivers. Free consultation. 45+ years of proven results. Call (734) 994-0200."
>
  <ArticleContent title="Safeguarding Pedestrians: Your Injury Advocates In Ann Arbor">
    <p>Pedestrian accidents are among the most distressing traffic incidents in Ann Arbor, often resulting in severe injuries or fatalities. The bustling streets, while full of life, can pose significant risks for those on foot, especially in areas with heavy traffic or inadequate pedestrian infrastructure. At Logeman &amp; Iafrate, P.C., we are committed to standing up for the rights of pedestrians who have been injured due to negligence or unsafe conditions.</p>

    <p>Our firm believes that every pedestrian deserves safe passage throughout Ann Arbor and beyond. Whether you've been hit by a distracted driver, faced harm due to poorly maintained walkways, or suffered in a crosswalk accident, our experienced attorneys are here to help. We understand the physical, emotional and financial toll these accidents can take, and we strive to provide compassionate, effective legal representation to ease your burden.</p>

    <h2>Strong Advocacy For Pedestrian Accident Victims In Ann Arbor</h2>
    <p>In the bustling streets of Ann Arbor, the presence of pedestrians, in-line skaters and various non-motorized vehicles adds vibrancy and diversity to our urban tapestry. However, this increase in street activity can sometimes lead to catastrophic outcomes, particularly when drivers become distracted rather than more vigilant.</p>

    <p>When a pedestrian is struck by a vehicle, the consequences can be severe and life-altering. Unlike motorists in <a href="/motor-vehicle-accidents-overview/">cars or other vehicles</a>, pedestrians have no barriers to shield them from the impact, making them vulnerable to <a href="/catastrophic-injuries-overview/">serious injuries</a> such as head trauma, paralysis, spinal cord injuries, or even fatal outcomes. Surprisingly, many drivers involved in such incidents may continue without realizing the severity of the collision.</p>

    <h2>Overcoming Challenges In Pedestrian Accident Claims</h2>
    <p>Pedestrian accidents often occur in situations where drivers fail to yield at crosswalks, despite Michigan laws mandating they do so. The distraction caused by everyday activities often leads to these dangerous encounters, highlighting the need for greater awareness and stricter adherence to traffic regulations.</p>

    <p>It's not uncommon for insurance companies and even juries to presume the pedestrian is at fault in accident scenarios. Our attorneys at Logeman &amp; Iafrate, P.C., are well-versed in shifting this narrative, demonstrating through clear evidence and expert testimony that the pedestrian was wronged and deserves just compensation.</p>

    <h2>Protecting Your Rights After A Hit-And-Run Accident</h2>
    <p>The complexity increases in hit-and-run accidents, where the responsible party flees the scene. Even in these challenging cases, victims may still have recourse through no-fault insurance policies, potentially including those held by other household members. Identifying and accessing these resources swiftly is crucial for covering medical expenses and other losses.</p>

    <h2>Legal Support Tailored To Your Needs</h2>
    <p>At Logeman &amp; Iafrate, P.C., we dedicate our knowledge and years of experience to ensure that each pedestrian accident victim receives full and fair compensation. From gathering critical evidence to negotiating with insurers and, if necessary, advocating in court, our team is committed to your recovery in every aspect.</p>

    <p>If you or a loved one has been involved in a pedestrian accident, prompt action is essential. By securing legal representation early, you safeguard your rights and enhance your chances of a favorable outcome. Our free consultations provide an opportunity to explore your options and plan your next steps without any initial financial commitment.</p>

    <h2>Contact Us Today For A Free Consultation</h2>
    <p>Our team is ready to assist clients in Ann Arbor, Detroit and throughout Michigan. Whether you are dealing with the aftermath of a pedestrian accident or seeking guidance on related injury claims, Logeman &amp; Iafrate, P.C., is here to support you. Contact us anytime to start your journey toward justice and healing by calling <a href="tel:+17342284339">(734) 228-4339</a> or by filling out our <a href="/contact-us/">online contact form</a>.</p>

    <p>We are committed to helping you recover the compensation you deserve for your pain, suffering and economic losses. Reach out today to learn how we can assist you in navigating the complexities of your pedestrian accident claim.</p>
  </ArticleContent>

  <ArticleFAQ items={faqItems} />

  <ArticleStats />

  <FreeConsultationForm />

  <Testimonials />

  <LocationMap />
</BaseLayout>
